<Base title="Contact" description="Contact Talha M Blog: email contact@talhablog.com for corrections, right of reply, copyright and privacy requests, feedback and story suggestions.">
  <section class="article-head"><h1>Contact</h1></section>
  <div class="prose">
<p><em>Last updated: October 16, 2026 — 11:53 PM (Pakistan time)</em></p>
    <p>Talha M Blog is a small, independent website, run by one person. Email is the best and fastest way to reach us. We welcome corrections, topic suggestions, questions and honest feedback.</p>

    <h2>Our email address</h2>
    <p><b>contact@talhablog.com</b></p>
    <p><a href="mailto:contact@talhablog.com?subject=Message%20for%20Talha%20M%20Blog">Tap here to write an email</a>. Please write a clear subject line — for example "Correction", "Copyright", "Privacy", "Story suggestion" or "Business" — so we can understand your message quickly and deal with urgent matters first. There is no contact form on this website; contact is by email only.</p>

    <h2>What you can write to us about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Corrections:</b> Tell us which article contains a mistake, include its link if you can, and explain what should be corrected. We will check it against reliable sources, and if we make a correction we will mark the article as updated.</li>
      <li><b>Right of reply:</b> If a story is about you or your organisation and you believe it is wrong, incomplete or unfair, send us your response. Where it is fair, we will correct the story or add your response. This is also explained in our <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Feedback:</b> Tell us what was useful, what was difficult to understand, or what could be improved. Feedback about confusing words or passages is especially helpful, because this website is written for readers of every level of English.</li>
      <li><b>Story suggestions:</b> Suggest a news story, a famous person's life story, a phone, an AI tool, a sports record, or another topic you would like explained in simple English. We cannot promise to cover every suggestion, but every suggestion is read.</li>
      <li><b>Questions about a post:</b> If something in a story is unclear, ask us, and we will try to explain it — or update the post where that would help other readers too.</li>
      <li><b>Copyright and takedown requests:</b> If you believe text or an image on this website uses your material without permission, email us with the details listed below. Copyright messages are checked as a priority. The same process is described in our <a href="/terms/">Terms of Use</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Privacy requests:</b> You can ask us to delete a comment you made, to remove your email address from the newsletter list, or to delete other information connected with you. Use the subject "Privacy", and tell us which comment or which email address your request is about. You can also unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time through the link in any newsletter email. Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what information we hold and the choices you have.</li>
      <li><b>Comments help:</b> If a comment does not appear, or you want your own comment removed, send us the story link and the name you commented with, so we can look into it.</li>
      <li><b>Technical problems:</b> If a page does not open, an image does not load, or installing the app does not work, tell us your device, your browser and what happened, so we can reproduce the problem.</li>
      <li><b>Business and advertising:</b> For genuine business questions, use the subject "Business". Please note: we never accept payment to change, hide or remove a news story.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to send a copyright request</h2>
    <p>Please include these four things in your email:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your full name, and the name of the owner of the material if that is a different person.</li>
      <li>The exact address (URL) of the page on talhablog.com where the material appears.</li>
      <li>A short description of your material and, if possible, a link to where it was first published.</li>
      <li>A statement that you own the material, or are authorised to act for its owner, and that its use on this website is not permitted.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We aim to reply to complete copyright requests within a few working days. If a request checks out, we will remove or correct the material as quickly as reasonably possible, and we will email you back. If you sent a request by mistake, or you later give permission, contact us again and we will restore the material where appropriate.</p>

    <h2>When will you get a reply?</h2>
    <p>We read every genuine email. The website is run by one person — so replies are not instant and can sometimes take a few days, especially when many messages arrive together. Corrections, right-of-reply and copyright messages are checked first. Please do not send the same message again and again; one clear email is enough.</p>

    <h2>Please do not send</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Passwords, bank details, card numbers or other private financial information. We will never ask you for these.</li>
      <li>Spam, chain messages or unrelated advertisements.</li>
      <li>Abusive or threatening messages. Honest criticism is always welcome; abusive messages may be deleted without a reply.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Other ways to follow us</h2>
    <p>You can find our latest posts on the homepage, follow Talha M Blog on Instagram at <a href="https://www.instagram.com/talh_ablog" rel="noopener" target="_blank">@talh_ablog</a>, read about the writer on our <a href="/author/">Author page</a>, and subscribe to the free email newsletter on any story page. You can also read more about the website on our <a href="/about/">About page</a>. For everything else — corrections, questions, suggestions and business — email remains the surest way to reach us. Thank you for reading, and for writing to Talha M Blog.</p>

  </div>
</Base>
